diff --git a/docs/gateway/config-extensions.md b/docs/gateway/config-extensions.md
index d4edcbda7e00397e366553b585303cb169c94200..8155dd92f5d25e72f70ade42117bd28e54ee1690 100644
--- a/docs/gateway/config-extensions.md
+++ b/docs/gateway/config-extensions.md
@@ -7,10 +7,42 @@ read_when:
 title: "Configuration — MCP, skills, and plugins"
 ---
 
-Extension surfaces: `mcp.*`, `skills.*`, `plugins.*`, and `canvas.*`.
+Extension surfaces: `mcp.*`, `skills.*`, `plugins.*`, `marketplace.*`, and `canvas.*`.
 
 For the full key index and the other top-level config domains, see [Configuration reference](/gateway/configuration-reference).
 
+## Marketplace
+
+Native marketplace integration is enabled by default. To opt out:
+
+```json5
+{
+  marketplace: { enabled: false },
+}
+```
+
+Restart the Gateway after changing this setting, then reload the Control UI.
+With integration disabled:
+
+- Plugin and skill discovery pages, marketplace recommendations, and ClawHub
+  invitations are hidden. Installed plugin and local skill settings remain available.
+- Native ClawHub search, downloads, verification, and promotions are unavailable.
+  Official-catalog and manifest-marketplace plugin acquisition is rejected, including
+  direct Gateway and CLI requests. Catalog caches are not a fallback.
+- Marketplace-backed plugin updates are skipped, preserving the installed copy.
+- Explicit npm packages, Git/local plugin sources, local skills, and configured MCP
+  servers remain available with their existing permissions and install checks.
+
+This setting controls OpenClaw's native integration. It does not remove bundled
+packages, restrict shell commands, or configure independent tools and agent harnesses.
+Those require their own packaging and policy choices. Existing installation provenance
+may still identify ClawHub; disabling integration does not rewrite that history.
+
+Provider/channel setup lists and plugin-authoring publishing templates are not
+curated by this setting. Catalog-selected remote installs from setup are still
+blocked. CLI help continues to describe marketplace commands, whose execution
+requires integration to be enabled.
+
 ## MCP
 
 OpenClaw-managed MCP server definitions live under `mcp.servers` for embedded
